# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Node / web UI
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Local development
.env
.env.local
*.local

# Recordings and other media produced while testing, which must never be
# committed: they are large and can contain whatever was on screen.
/recordings/
*.mkv
*.mp4
*.wav

# What the installer carries beside the window: a release recorder and the
# FFmpeg DLLs it links, put there by scripts/stage-installer-payload.ps1
# (issue #226). Build outputs, and 143 MB of them. The directory itself is
# created by apps/desktop/src-tauri/build.rs, because tauri.conf.json declares
# it as a bundle resource and a declared resource that does not exist fails
# every build of that crate.
/apps/desktop/src-tauri/installer-payload/

# Prebuilt FFmpeg, fetched by scripts/fetch-ffmpeg.ps1. It is pinned to an
# immutable release asset and checksum-verified on every fetch, so the bytes are
# reproducible without a 67 MB download - 168 MB extracted - living in git
# history.
/third-party/ffmpeg/

# The corresponding source of the pinned FFmpeg, when it is assembled here
# rather than at scripts/fetch-ffmpeg-source.ps1's default of
# third-party/ffmpeg/source. .github/workflows/release.yml puts it here on
# purpose, to keep it out of the directory the FFmpeg cache restores, and it is
# 22 MB of somebody else's source that a release publishes as assets rather than
# something to keep in this history.
/ffmpeg-source/

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local agent worktrees. These are real git checkouts of this repository, so
# committing them would embed a repository inside itself.
/.claude/worktrees/

# One developer's own agent settings and scratch space. `settings.json` beside
# them is shared and is committed; these two are not.
/.claude/settings.local.json
/.claude/scratch/
